# Git

Do **not** use the global HEREDOC-body / parallel-git commit playbook in this repo.

1. `working_directory` = **this** repo root (`…/mcp-gateway`). Never `ethereumjs-monorepo`, never `feelyourprotocol/`.
2. Every git command: `required_permissions: ["all"]`. An error about `packages/ethereum-tests/.git` means you ran git in the monorepo — re-run with 1+2.
3. Commits, pushes, pulls, and `gh pr create` are **one shell at a time** (Touch ID). Never parallel signed git, even across FYP siblings.
4. Commit message: **one line**, ~7–10 words, no `feat:` / `fix:`, **no body**.

Full habits (when, scope, CI, PRs): sibling [`../website/.cursor/rules/git.mdc`](../website/.cursor/rules/git.mdc) (canonical). Do not fork a second long copy here.
